## The findings

````findings
1. [crates/opencompany-core/src/harness/built_in/chargebee.rs] Change import to wrong crate alias that breaks all uses
The old import `use openhuman_core::openhuman as oh;` makes `oh` refer to the `openhuman` **module** inside `openhuman_core`. The new import `use openhuman_core as oh;` makes `oh` refer to the **crate root** itself, which has a different set of public items. Every subsequent `oh::` path in this file (e.g. `oh::tools::traits::{PermissionLevel, Tool, ToolResult}` on line 120 and `oh::tools::traits::PermissionLevel` on line 546) now resolves against the crate root, not the `openhuman` module, so the code will not compile.
